.retry` 600s-scale retry logic), which only succeeded on a later retry at 22:42 — confirmed live: the containerd task for that domain is now RUNNING (PID 9174, started ~22:42:52), the QMP socket/pidfile now exist, and `app-info` shows the app actually reached `RUNNING` with an IP. The evetest harness's 10-minute wait, however, had already expired before this successful retry landed, so the test timed out despite the app having eventually come up — this looks like a one-off transient QEMU/launch glitch on the first attempt (no kernel OOM, no dmesg errors, no permission denials found) rather than a logic bug in the retry path itself. This is not shared with any other failure in this run and doesn't match anything in the ledger — no entry for `TestHardwareSuite`/`TestUSBFlashDriveHotplug` or this QMP-socket symptom appears there, so this is a new failure, not a previously known recurring one.","time":{"start":1793916866000,"stop":1793918638010,"duration":1772010}},{"uid":"ae9953422e9b7dd8","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/8/#testresult/ae9953422e9b7dd8","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793836924000,"stop":1793837364610,"duration":440610}}]},"tags":[]},"source":"ef6d28ca917677ab.json","parameterValues":[]}